  "title": "The automobile age",
  "summary": "Ford's breakthrough came in 1908 with the Model T, built for efficiency, reliability and a reasonable price. At its Highland Park plant in Michigan, Ford introduced assembly-line mass production, with each worker staying in one place while vehicles passed by. In 1926 the United States launched its first federal highway system, including Route 66.",
